{
guid:"{8DE98199-38B3-4CC6-8744-63DB2FBA7781}",
title:"Enter the relational population through the CaseTalk population editor",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 093151.973",
modified:"20260905 173027.771",
priority:"High",
category:"Testing",
completed:"True",
text:"The MCP population tool assigns values to LEXICAL roles only, so only the identification fact types could be populated from here (Country, Local Area, Branch, Car Group, Car Model, Car, Person, Rental instances exist). Fact types with an object-type role - Car Model of Car, Home Branch of Car, Renter of Rental, Pick Up Branch, Car of Rental, Rental Tariff and the rest - still have no tuples. The intended sample dataset is written out in full in POPULATION.md in the project folder; enter it in the population editor, or import it once population import from file is available."
},
{
guid:"{77345F93-EECC-4EAD-82D3-16EE9F7B0021}",
title:"Re-code six glossary terms from Label type back to Concept",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 093152.212",
modified:"20260905 173029.080",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Validation",
completed:"True",
text:"EU-Rent, Authorized Area, Car Group Upgrade, Car Transfer, Rental Agreement and Scheduled Service were created as Concepts, but linking them to an object type with add_role intent=related demoted them to Label types, and nothing can promote a Label back. They now carry a char(60) datatype only so the well-formedness check passes. Change their code back to Concept in the OTFT editor; their definitions and sources are intact."
},
{
guid:"{0ECE1606-C654-435A-B480-7CFEF779339E}",
title:"Write derivation expressions for the ten rules that are not structural",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 093153.187",
modified:"20260905 173030.402",
priority:"High",
category:"Enhancement",
completed:"True",
text:"R03 (at most three additional drivers), R04 (barred driver), R05 (licence still valid at return date), R06 (driver at least 21 at pick-up), R07 (rental period at most 90 days), R09 (location penalty when drop-off differs from pick-up), R12/R13 (upgrade to a higher car group), R14 (5000 mile service interval), R18 (late return penalty) and R19 (three bad experiences bar a driver) are stated in each rule's [Definition] but nothing enforces them. Each needs a derivation or constraint expression, or explicit application logic. R01, R02, R08, R16 and R17 ARE enforced structurally - their annotations say which constraint does it."
},
{
guid:"{28E13F9C-67AD-4C4B-8ABC-F1DA3FCCC4A6}",
title:"Confirm the fact type expressions with a domain expert",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 093153.562",
modified:"20260828 093153.562",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Review",
completed:"False",
text:"All 43 fact type expressions and the generated object type expressions are still unconfirmed - the well-formedness check reports 64 &quot;expression is generated, requires validated semantics&quot; warnings. The wordings come from the published EU-Rent sources, not from an interview, so they are deliberately left unconfirmed. Walk the expression list with a domain expert and set confirmed=yes where the wording is agreed."
},
{
guid:"{C1749887-F08F-41DA-842E-2F9612203633}",
title:"Three thresholds are assumed, not sourced - check with the business",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 093154.887",
modified:"20260828 093154.887",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Question",
completed:"False",
text:"The published EU-Rent material does not fix these numbers, so the model states a plausible value and says so in the rule annotation: R06 minimum driver age 21, R07 maximum rental period 90 days, R19 three bad experiences before a driver is barred. Confirm each, or replace it with the value EU-Rent actually uses. Also open: whether a maximum driver age applies, and whether the bad-experience count should be per period rather than lifetime."
},
{
guid:"{2299E7AD-612D-401C-A8D7-0CE62CCD455C}",
title:"Model the areas the case study leaves out",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 093157.590",
modified:"20260828 093157.590",
priority:"Low",
category:"Enhancement",
completed:"False",
text:"Deliberately out of scope in this pass, listed in paragraph &quot;2. Scope Of This Model&quot;: reservation inventory and availability forecasting (needed before R12, the free upgrade, can be evaluated at all), accident and insurance claim handling, invoicing and payment settlement, and the loyalty/incentive scheme that later versions of EU-Rent add. Decide which of these the model should grow into."
},
{
