completed:"True",
text:"population {&quot;operation&quot;:&quot;export&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;xlsx&quot;,&quot;oftypename&quot;:&quot;Name of Country&quot;,&quot;filepath&quot;:&quot;nameofcountry.xlsx&quot;} returned: Export failed: Access violation at address 0000464400000000 in module CaseTalk.exe. CSV export answers &quot;not yet implemented. Use format=xlsx for now&quot;, so there is currently no working population export path through MCP. Reproduced 2026-08-28 on the EU-Rent model."
},
{
guid:"{6316AC9F-98EE-4834-A0B4-615F551A4F2D}",
title:"MCP add_role intent=related creates an unnamed fact type between the two types",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 094011.063",
modified:"20260905 173031.640",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Validation",
completed:"True",
text:"Six fact types &quot;Rental - Rental Agreement&quot;, &quot;Local Area - Authorized Area&quot;, &quot;Car Group - Car Group Upgrade&quot;, &quot;Car - Scheduled Service&quot;, &quot;Car - Car Transfer&quot; and &quot;Branch - EU-Rent&quot; were created as a side effect of relating a glossary concept to an object type. They arrive with no uniqueness constraint (well-formedness warning) and no population, and they demote the concept to a Label type. UCs have now been added by hand. Decide whether these six link fact types should stay at all, or whether the glossary terms belong in a container instead."
},
{
guid:"{E44521DE-A87A-44DC-8E02-9E45387421BD}",
title:"Model documentation lives in doc/, not in the project folder",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 094331.297",
modified:"20260828 095112.118",
priority:"Low",
category:"Documentation",
completed:"True",
text:"Saving the project sweeps loose files out of the project folder into &quot;unused files.zip&quot; and regenerates README.md, so the hand-written docs (MODEL.md, VOCABULARY.md, RULES.md, POPULATION.md, SOURCES.md, SESSION-NOTES.md) were moved to doc/. Start at doc/MODEL.md. Do not put markdown back in the project root - it will be swept on the next save."
},
{
guid:"{0E566FCF-C688-494C-8795-05C8F110FF6A}",
title:"Model documentation is in doc/, registered as project members",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260828 095115.568",
modified:"20260905 173032.656",
priority:"Low",
category:"Documentation",
completed:"True",
text:"Six markdown documents live in doc/ and are attached to the project with markdown_file operation=register: MODEL.md (start here), VOCABULARY.md, RULES.md, POPULATION.md, SOURCES.md and SESSION-NOTES.md. All except SESSION-NOTES are flagged in_report, so they are pulled into the generated project (MIM) report. Anything added later must be registered the same way - an unregistered file in the project folder is swept into &quot;unused files.zip&quot; on the next save, and README.md is regenerated by CaseTalk, so do not hand-edit it."
},
{
guid:"{9E5F7EF7-7843-4939-8E3C-0A1B601A6436}",
title:"Counter-example rentals 10004-10008 carry only the fact they violate",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260905 173341.619",
modified:"20260905 173341.619",
priority:"Low",
category:"Testing",
completed:"False",
text:"The counter-examples from POPULATION.md are in the repository as tuples flagged is_counter_example (Main Driver of Rental 10004, Additional Driver 10005 x4, Rental Period 10006, Car of Rental 10007 and 10008, Requested Car Group 10008, Rental Tariff B/NL 55.00). Each creates a Rental instance that has none of its mandatory facts (renter, pick-up branch, state ...), so the totality constraints on Rental are unmet for those five instances. Decide whether to give them a full set of facts, or to accept that a counter-example documents one forbidden tuple and nothing more. The Car Model counter-example (a second &quot;Opel / Astra&quot;) is not entered: Car Model is now identified by its own expression, so a duplicate is simply the same instance."
},
{
guid:"{AFDB7342-44E6-4CE5-B89D-4C8EDD17674C}",
title:"Review the [Derivation] annotations on R03-R19 and pick a formal notation",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260905 173344.912",
modified:"20260905 173344.912",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Review",
completed:"False",
text:"The behavioural rules R03, R04, R05, R06, R07, R09, R11, R12, R13, R14, R18 and R19 now carry a [Derivation] section written in a role-path pseudo-notation (FOR EACH Rental R: COUNT(Additional Driver[R]) &lt;= 3, etc.), and the four derived Rental subtypes are flagged derivable with their defining condition. They are readable and reviewable, but not executable. Decide on the target notation (SBVR Structured English, OCL, SQL over the generated schema, or CaseTalk's own derivation syntax with &lt;math&gt; blocks) and rewrite them once, so that the rules can be checked against the population mechanically."
},
{
guid:"{7C3319D8-BDB5-4656-9DC1-CF26EEA02DB6}",
title:"Delete the eight unused wordy object type expressions O3-O10",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260905 173350.866",
modified:"20260905 173350.866",
priority:"Low",
category:"Validation",
completed:"False",
text:"When the identification was repaired (role repointed from &quot;Country ID&quot; to &quot;Country Code&quot; and so on), substitutions fix_missing created a bare identifying expression per object type (&quot;&lt;Country Code&gt;&quot;, &quot;&lt;Manufacturer&gt; &lt;Model Name&gt;&quot; ...) and pointed every substitution at it. The older wordy readings - O3 &quot;country &lt;Country Code&gt;&quot;, O4 &quot;local area &lt;Local Area Code&gt;&quot;, O5 &quot;branch &lt;Branch Code&gt;&quot;, O6 &quot;car group &lt;Car Group Code&gt;&quot;, O7 &quot;car model &lt;Manufacturer&gt; &lt;Model Name&gt;&quot;, O8 &quot;car &lt;Registration Number&gt;&quot;, O9 &quot;person &lt;Person Number&gt;&quot;, O10 &quot;rental &lt;Rental Number&gt;&quot; - are now unused and the well-formedness check says so (8 warnings). Delete them in the expression editor, or run delete_element target=expression through the MCP and click Allow in the consent dialog (the MCP delete permission is set to ask, and the 2026-09-05 session could not get past that prompt). Alternatively keep the wordy ones and repoint the substitutions, which gives verbalisations like &quot;country NL is named Netherlands&quot;."
},
{
guid:"{9EB6061B-A074-4E81-91C6-525D18D9D757}",
title:"Model the fleet disposal rule from the original case: sold at one year old or 40,000 km",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260907 182651.847",
modified:"20260908 092304.445",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Enhancement",
completed:"True",
text:"The 1995 GUIDE / Business Rules Group report (Appendix D, EU-Rent Car Rentals, by Model Systems Ltd.) states that cars are to be sold when they reach one year old or 40,000 kilometres, whichever comes first. The model has no purchase date or age for a Car, and the odometer is in miles (the 5000-mile service interval comes from the later SBVR retelling). Add a Car purchase/registration date fact, decide on the unit of Mileage, add a Condition state for a car sold or withdrawn, and write the rule as R21 with a derivation over Car Odometer Reading and the new date."
},
{
guid:"{BFCE5D1E-111A-4F13-A346-C1E08CA200A1}",
title:"Model "one car on rental at a time" and "the signing driver has no car out" from the original case",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260907 182655.502",
modified:"20260907 183148.781",
priority:"Medium",
category:"Enhancement",
completed:"True",
text:"Two rules from the original 1995 case study (Business Rules Group report, Appendix D) are not among R01-R20: a customer can have several reservations but only one car rented at a time, and the driver who signs the rental agreement must not currently have an EU-Rent car on rental. Both are derivations over Open Rental joined with Renter of Rental / Main Driver of Rental (at most one Open Rental per Customer; no Open Rental for the main driver at pick-up). Add them as R22 and R23 in the EU-Rent Business Rules container with [Definition], [Source] and [Derivation], and add a counter-example to the population."
},
{
guid:"{295F7AC1-EE2C-4C26-9F56-046DB0F67F56}",
title:"Decide whether the EU-Corporation context of the original case belongs in the model",
bookmark:"",
user:"marcowobben",
created:"20260907 182700.044",
modified:"20260907 182700.044",
priority:"Low",
category:"Question",
completed:"False",
text:"The original 1995 case study places EU-Rent inside EU-Corporation next to EU-Fly (airline) and EU-Stay (hotels) with a shared customer base, gives it 1000 branches, and adds service depots that each serve several branches and take maintenance bookings subject to capacity. None of this is in the model: there is no Service Depot, Car Service hangs directly off Car, and Person is EU-Rent's own. Decide whether to add Service Depot (with Car Service performed at a depot and a depot serving a Local Area or Branch), and whether the shared-customer aspect is in scope at all or belongs with the out-of-scope areas listed in paragraph 2."
}
